      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The wiki has a clear answer to your question:\n\n**The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by never loading the key into it in the first place.** According to [[credential-scoping]], a local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and injects it directly into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process\u2014the Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated with this credential.\n\nThis design has a key security benefit: even if the Hub process itself is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the API key by inspecting its own environment variables, since the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually uses it. The same scoping model applies to the Query agent as well\u2014it also receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn time, never inherited from the Hub.",
